' 4+1 logical view - Logical view · back end layers (Clean Architecture)
' Version 1.1 - 2026-11-10
' For: whoever writes the code.
' Documented decision: Clean Architecture in the back end: dependencies point inward only (Api → Infrastructure → Application → Domain).
' Not drawn: individual classes.
@startuml logical-layers
!include ../style.puml

title Logical view - back end layers (Clean Architecture)


package "ASP.NET Core API" as C_API {
  component "SportsBooking.Api\n[ASP.NET Core, controllers]" as L_API
  component "SportsBooking.Infrastructure\n[EF Core, Npgsql, Identity, MailKit]" as L_INF
  component "SportsBooking.Application\n[FluentValidation, EF Core (DbSet and LINQ, no\nNpgsql)]" as L_APP
  component "SportsBooking.Domain\n[C# with no dependencies]" as L_DOM
}

L_API --> L_INF : References and composes\n[AddInfrastructure(config)]
L_API --> L_APP : Calls the services\n[AddApplication(), transitive reference]
L_INF --> L_APP : Implements the interfaces\n[IAppDbContext, IBookingStore, IPitchLock,\nISessionService, IEmailSender…]
L_APP --> L_DOM : Uses the entities and the rules\n[project reference]

note right of L_INF
  **Real exceptions**
  Persisted entities outside Domain:
  AppUser, RefreshToken
  and OwnerStatusChange in Infrastructure.
  Identity's password-reset token generator
  reads the system clock, not TimeProvider.
end note

note right of L_APP
  **Real exception**
  OutboxMessage is a persisted entity
  that lives in Application.
end note

note right of L_DOM
  Domain references no project
  and no package; it knows neither EF Core nor HTTP.
end note
@enduml
